# Change-feed text search plan

## Module structure

- `crates/shared/src/change_feed.rs` remains the shared HTTP query contract. Add
  an optional `q` field and a normalization helper so blank, whitespace-only,
  and absent values are all represented as no search.
- `crates/backend/src/feed.rs` consumes that normalized value and adds a
  parameterized, case-insensitive title-or-change-summary predicate to the
  existing candidate query. The existing filters remain ANDed together, while
  the title/summary match is grouped as one OR condition.
- `frontend/src/api/client.ts` owns the `ChangeFeedFilters` wire type and query
  serialization; it gains optional `q` support. `frontend/src/api/hooks.ts`
  continues to use the complete filter object as the query key.
- `frontend/src/pages/ChangeFeedPage.tsx` owns the URL-backed `q` state and
  passes it through to the query hook. `frontend/src/components/FeedFilterBar.tsx`
  owns the dense search input and its debounced change callback.

## Issue dependency

1. Issue #103 first: define `q` in the shared DTO, normalize it, bind it in
   SQL, and cover blank/absent plus title and summary matching behavior without
   altering sort, limit/offset, or `next_offset` semantics.
2. Issue #104 then: add the debounced search box, keep `q` in the browser URL,
   include it in client requests/query identity and clear/reset behavior, and
   preserve paging/count behavior for the filtered result set.

## Key design decisions

- Use `q` as the one wire name across API, URL parameters, and TypeScript
  filters to avoid mapping drift.
- Trim only to detect an empty search; pass a normal query as a bound value and
  use PostgreSQL case-insensitive matching against `entries.title` and
  `latest.change_summary` with `COALESCE` for nullable summaries.
- Keep search conjunctive with region, agency, status, and category; do not
  change deduplication or pagination.
- Debounce only the UI update that writes `q` to URL state. The URL remains the
  durable source of truth, making searches reload-safe and shareable while the
  React Query key naturally resets pagination when the committed term changes.
